#### 4. iOS Gemma model delivery: `GemmaBackgroundAssetsBridge.swift` does not exist
**Files:** [GemmaBaseModelInstaller.ios.kt:15-20](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PDFParser/shared/src/iosMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/insights/gemma/GemmaBaseModelInstaller.ios.kt#L15-L20), [GemmaModelPaths.ios.kt:25-26](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PDFParser/shared/src/iosMain/kotlin/com/payslipmax/pdfparser/insights/gemma/GemmaModelPaths.ios.kt#L25-L26)

The Kotlin side (`IosGemmaBaseModelInstaller`) is complete and wired to `progressReporter`/`completionReporter` companion slots. But the Swift file that is supposed to call those slots — `GemmaBackgroundAssetsBridge.swift` — **does not exist** in the `iosApp/iosApp/` directory. The App Group entitlement and Background Assets extension Xcode target also haven't been created. On a real non-debug device, Tier 6 (on-device AI) **will always stay in `NotStarted` state** for iOS users.

Whether we should undertake #1 right now depends on your **Apple Developer Program membership status**:

### Scenario A: You ALREADY have an active Apple Developer Account
**Yes, we should do it now.**
We can:
1. Write `GemmaBackgroundAssetsBridge.swift` and connect it to `AppDelegate`.
2. Open Xcode, add the **Background Assets Extension** target, enable the **App Group entitlement**, and configure `Info.plist`.
3. Build and test on a physical device / TestFlight.

---

### Scenario B: You DO NOT YET have an active Apple Developer Account
**We can write the Swift bridge code, but we cannot finish the Xcode configuration.**
* **Why?** Xcode will reject enabling **App Group entitlements** and signing the **Background Assets Extension** target without an active Apple Developer account provisioning profile.
* **Recommendation:** 
  - We can draft `GemmaBackgroundAssetsBridge.swift` now so the code side is 100% ready.
  - We hold on creating the Xcode target and entitlements until your Apple Developer account registration is complete.

---

What remains when you enroll in the Apple Developer Program:

- Open the project in Xcode (iosApp/iosApp.xcodeproj).
- Create the Background Assets Extension target (BADownloaderExtension).
- Enable the App Group entitlement (group.com.payslipmax.pdfparser.gemma) on both the main app and extension target.
- Add the required download URL keys to Info.plist.

⏳ What is PENDING (Xcode Target & Signing)
- The remaining work cannot be completed in code alone until your Apple Developer Account enrollment is active:
    - Background Assets Target: Adding the BADownloaderExtension target in Xcode.
    - App Group Entitlement: Enabling group.com.payslipmax.pdfparser.gemma on the app target (requires Apple Developer signing certificate).
